{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the ruler of the County of Tripoli from approximately 1102 until his death in 1152. He was the son of Pons II Count of Tripoli and the brother of William II Count of Tripoli.\n\n**Early Life and Reign**\n\nRaymond's early life details are not well documented however it is known that he played a significant role in the history of the County of Tripoli. He became the ruler of the county in 1102 following the death of his brother William II. At this time the county was facing significant challenges from the neighboring Seljuk Empire. Raymond III took various measures to strengthen the county's defenses including the construction of fortifications and the recruitment of mercenaries.\n\n**Religious Conflict and Crusades**\n\nRaymond III was also involved in the First Crusade and played a significant role in the capture of Jerusalem in 1099. He later became a prominent figure in the Second Crusade however his efforts were largely unsuccessful. In 1148 he attended the Second Crusade and fought alongside the forces of King Louis VII of France and Emperor Conrad III of Germany. \n\n**Relationships and Succession**\n\nRaymond III had several relationships including one with a woman named Izz al-Din Masud's sister who was a princess of the Seljuk Empire. She bore him a son named Raymond IV Count of Tripoli who would eventually succeed him as the ruler of the county.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0016098171472549438}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001308832288486883}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.16895784437656403}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.802703940891661e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0002967870968859643}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -7.068861305015162e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.008241336792707443}, {"token": " the", "logprob":